{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794209159,"nonce":"bdU5MiEGhuYqVHUB91oEZcJOcxI=","title":"Reader CSS: scoped \u003cstyle\u003e blocks per component instead of one global app.css","message":"All reader styles are in reader/src/app.css (about 1,700 lines), imported once in main.ts, and no .svelte file has a \u003cstyle\u003e block, so every rule is global. Svelte's convention is a \u003cstyle\u003e block in each component, scoped to it by a generated class, with only tokens (:root variables), resets and shared element styles (buttons, forms) global. Move component rules into their components in one PR; keep app.css for the tokens and shared styles. svelte-check --fail-on-warnings flags unused selectors in scoped styles, which catches dead CSS.","files":null}]}